# `ring[i & 15]`: the key lies between nothing and the mask, so whether it lies inside the list is one question for all turns: is the list longer than the mask. It was asked of the key in every turn.
# In front of the turns laid out the length is held against the mask once, and in those turns the read goes without its bound: a thousand turns 8,413 > 3,680 instructions, plain Bun 11,095.
# Who fails that question (a list of 100 read under `i & 255` by a counter that stays below 100) loses nothing but the question: behind these layouts stand the layouts as they were, which ask each key: 1,028 > 1,044.
# The first form of this asked in front of the typed copy of the walk, and who failed took the closed copy: 1,028 > 7,858.
# RUN: compile UnrolledLoopsForMaskedIndexes mechanisms=all
# CHECK: statistic UnrolledLoopsForMaskedIndexes {{*}}
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: 200 71.5 NaN 200 308 0 NaN
